    // ";;&" branches on to the NEXT clause's test after its body, ";&" falls into the next
    // clause's BODY without testing it, ";;" ends the case. The status is the last body
    // command's, 0 when no clause matched or the body is empty (`false; case x in x) ;; esac`
    // is 0). Twin of makeCase in bash-interpreter.abnf.
